From 62685f6f4e5208030b6713b5cec3681c98c7dcad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:11:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rd: frame generation (the camera between two game steps), its
 debug views

- interp.wgsl: the picture on screen moved to the camera of a moment between the last two game steps (smooth) or past the last
  one (predict), from its depth (one value per game pixel, copied when the 3D is finished: the copy after the most depth-tested
  drawing of the step) and the game's world-to-screen matrix of each step (exact: GS x, y, depth = the matrix's x/w, y/w, z/w)
- the step mark: host call 203 (camera frame) sends the matrix and the hero's limbs in order with the drawing (queue kInterpMark);
  the hero moves as one piece with the torso, the head's capsule gives the hair (no depth) the hero's depth; HUD boxes stay
- splats of 2x2 samples with a depth key, background samples beside nearer things and the rain's thin streaks left out, gaps
  filled from the farthest landed neighbour to the side; cuts (the screen's middle moving a quarter of the picture) skipped
- keys.ini frame_generation = off | smooth | predict, Settings > Display, the PC options row; PS2_FRAME_GEN at start
- Settings > Debug: what the made pictures show (the picture, gaps in magenta, depth moved), its log, save the next 6 pictures
  (PS2_PRESENT_DUMP=<vblank>,<base>[,<count>]: with SMAA's maps and frame generation's depth and keys)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
